    "description": "#145 (UD-Q4_K_M experts with routed downs, recurrent qkv/z/out, attention q/o of layers 11-39, lm_head and embeddings on Q4_K: RP-KL 0.1016, decode 474.3, 23.40 GiB) with every one of those kq_rtn tensors encoded by kq_imat (#138, merged): importance-weighted K-quant scales from the pinned statistics, no error feedback. Formats, kernels, speed and memory are #145's; only the rounding of 289 tensors changes. kq_imat lowers the weighted error of its tensors by 25-32% against kq_rtn (#138's measurements), so drift should fall at the fastest decode on the track. Unsloth's routed gate/up bytes stay.\n",
